# UI/UX BRAIN

## Hierarchy & Layout
- One primary action per view, visually dominant. Everything else is secondary (outline/ghost) or tertiary (text link).
- 8px spacing grid. Related things close, unrelated things far. Whitespace is information.
- Mobile-first, thumb-first: primary actions in the bottom half of the screen, minimum 44×44px touch targets, safe-area insets respected.
- Content max-width on large screens (~560-720px for focused apps). Never let text lines exceed ~70 characters.

## States (non-negotiable - every interactive element and every view)
- **Empty**: actionable, warm, points to the first step with a real button.
- **Loading**: skeleton or spinner appears after 200ms delay (not instantly - avoids flash).
- **Error**: plain-language cause + recovery action inline, near where the problem is.
- **Success**: confirmation the action landed (toast, checkmark, state change) within 100ms perceived.
- **Partial/zero-data**: charts and rings must look INTENTIONAL at zero, never broken. "Fresh day - log anything to start" beats an empty 0% ring.

## Interaction
- Everything the user can do must be DISCOVERABLE. No secret keyboard shortcuts as the only path, no hidden tap targets without a visual affordance (chevron, underline, dashed border).
- Tap-to-edit beats delete-and-retype. Inline editing for any value the user typed.
- Optimistic UI: update immediately, reconcile after. Never make the user wait for local operations.
- Animation: 150-300ms, ease-out, only on state changes the user caused, plus at most ONE signature moment per app. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (kill all animation).
- Celebrate real milestones (first entry, perfect day, streak records) - small, quick, never blocking.

## Visual craft
- Pick 4-6 named colors and NEVER introduce ad-hoc hex values outside the token set. Every color means one thing (green = habits, amber = money...). Semantic color consistency is navigation.
- Two font roles max (display + body), full weight scale used deliberately. Type hierarchy: size AND weight AND color change together between levels, never just one.
- Both light and dark themes from tokens - every token exists in both, no hardcoded colors in components.
- Border-radius, shadows, and border weights come from a scale (e.g. 8/12/16/20), never invented per-component.
- Numbers that matter get big type + small label. Labels are uppercase, small, tracked-out, muted.

## Accessibility (floor, not feature)
- Every icon-only button has `aria-label`. Every input has a label. Focus states visible. Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 body, ≥ 3:1 large text. Full keyboard path through every flow. Screen-reader-sensible DOM order.

